
<div class="row mt-2">
    <div class="col-12">
        <h4>Waking Resources</h4>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="row mt-1">
    <div class="col-10 offset-1">
        <p>
            For the best experience, start by ensuring all resources are awake by clicking on the 'API Resource Status' tab (next tab to the right), and then clicking ping all. Pinging resources does not require login.
            The Consumer client can be pinged or accessed from the 'Consumer Client App' tab.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<h4 class="mt-4">Nav Menu Items</h4>
<div class="row mt-2">
    <div class="col-10 offset-1">
        <h5>Store</h5>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="row mt-1">
    <div class="col-8 offset-2">
        <p>A replication of the Consumer Client storefront with full functionality.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mt-2">
    <div class="col-10 offset-1">
        <h5>Products Management</h5>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="row mt-1">
    <div class="col-8 offset-2">
        <p>
            The Product Management page allows adding product images and documents. Additional pages display Product Write Side API data collections, to include
            Event Store records, Outbox records, and any generated snapshots.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mt-2">
    <div class="col-10 offset-1">
        <h5>Claims</h5>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="row mt-1">
    <div class="col-8 offset-2">
        <p>
            Retrieves user claims from the various API resources and displays them in the client.  Also allows viewing the client claims.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mt-2">
    <div class="col-10 offset-1">
        <h5>Developers</h5>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="row mt-1">
    <div class="col-8 offset-2">
        <p>
            Generate errors in the Product Write Side API and returns the generated problem details response.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

